PROVENANCE
----------

Every container image in the ACE project is built from upstream, Apache-2.0
licensed source, cloned at a pinned commit at build time:

  ansible/jewel, ansible/ansible-ui, ansible/awx, ansible/galaxy_ng,
  ansible/eda-server, ansible/receptor, ansible/django-ansible-base

Red Hat's own distribution of this platform was examined as a BEHAVIORAL
SPECIFICATION only: to learn what the official images and installer produce,
so that an equivalent end state could be written independently. Observing a
released artifact and describing what it does is the whole of that exercise.

No Red Hat file, template, role, playbook, manifest, or configuration has
been copied into this project, and no vendor distribution is redistributed
by it.

FILESYSTEM PATHS
----------------

Some filesystem paths retain vendor-derived names — /opt/aap-gateway,
/etc/ansible-automation-platform/, /var/lib/ansible-automation-platform/.
These are deliberate and are a compatibility decision, not a claim of
association: upstream tooling, shipped scripts and management commands
resolve them, and renaming them would mean forking the upstream projects
this software is built from.

Identifiers such as aap-gateway-manage, aap_gateway_api, aap-eda-manage,
/etc/tower and /var/lib/awx come from the upstream Apache-2.0 projects
themselves and are used unchanged.
